NOTICE — CoC 7e Fair Use Declaration
====================================

coc-keeper is an open-source AI Keeper skill for the Hermes Agent ecosystem.
This notice clarifies the relationship between coc-keeper and the original
*Call of Cthulhu* tabletop role-playing game by Chaosium Inc.


1. WHAT COC-KEEPER USES
-----------------------

coc-keeper references **core mechanical concepts** from the *Call of
Cthulhu* 7th Edition Keeper Rulebook (published by Chaosium Inc.),
including but not limited to:

  - The d100 / percentile dice mechanic
  - Skill check resolution (regular / hard / extreme success, fumble,
    critical success thresholds)
  - The SAN (Sanity) attribute and SAN check procedure
  - The bout-of-madness mechanic and its tables
  - The clue / investigation structure of scenarios

These references appear as **prompt engineering material** — the AI
Keeper is told *how* the rules work so it can adjudicate player actions.


2. WHAT COC-KEEPER DOES NOT INCLUDE
-----------------------------------

  - **No module / scenario text** from any published CoC adventure
    (e.g. *The House on the Borderland*, *The Haunting*, *Masks of
    Nyarlathotep*, etc.). The two built-in scenarios
    (《山间怪屋》/ "Borderland" and 《沙漠驿站》/ "Solo Crypt") are
    **original** prompt-skeleton scenarios written specifically for
    this skill, not transcriptions of published Chaosium material.
  - **No full rulebook text** — only short, paraphrased references for
    the AI to follow.
  - **No artwork, character art, or trade dress** from Chaosium.


3. INTENDED USE
---------------

  - Free, non-commercial use by tabletop groups who already own the
    *Call of Cthulhu* rulebook and want an AI-assisted Keeper.
  - Educational / research use of the prompt engineering techniques
    demonstrated in SKILL.md and references/v2_design_notes.md.
  - NOT intended to replace the rulebook. Players and Keepers should
    own (or have access to) a physical / digital copy of the CoC 7e
    Keeper Rulebook for full gameplay.


4. NO AFFILIATION
-----------------

coc-keeper is an independent community project. It is **not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Chaosium Inc.** All references to
*Call of Cthulhu*, CoC, and related marks are for descriptive /
compatibility purposes only.


5. WHY THIS NOTICE EXISTS
-------------------------

  - Chaosium has a published *Call of Cthulhu* **Fair Use Policy**
    permitting community projects that follow the spirit of the rules
    without redistributing protected text. coc-keeper follows that
    policy.
  - This file is the only place where the above is stated explicitly.
    README, SKILL.md, and other docs refer back to this NOTICE
    rather than restating it.


For the upstream Fair Use Policy, see:
https://www.chaosium.com/blog/a-fair-use-policy-for-call-of-cthulhu/
